// proves the sibling-floor fix natively too: a `@derive`d quote's
// SECOND top-level declaration (a generic-seat-taking `stores(...)`
// call, wrapping a LAMBDA answering a generic `Rows<R>`) once left the
// FIRST's `once fn` reading corrupted facts — clean under the
// evaluator, and "Function return type does not match operand type
// of return inst!" from LLVM under `avra build`, in the lambda's own
// lifted body.
use @std.meta.{derive}
use @test.sibling_floor_native.{MakesRows}

@derive(MakesRows)
type Foo = { x: int }

"${Foo.read_count()}"
